1. **Convert the concentration to milligrams per milliliter (mg/mL):**
   - The concentration is 0.044% (w/v), which means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 100 milliliters of solution.
   - Convert this to mg/mL:
     \[
     \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} \times \frac{1000 \text{ mg}}{1 \text{ g}} = 0.44 \text{ mg/mL}
