","A **space group** is a fundamental concept in crystallography that describes the symmetry of a crystal structure. It is the set of all atoms in the crystal that can be placed in the same position as another atom in the crystal due to the symmetry of the crystal structure. This symmetry is preserved by the same set of operations.  

The symmetry of a crystal structure is more complex than the symmetry of a single unit plane (e as in crystallography). The symmetry of a crystal includes the symmetry of the crystal lattice (the arrangement of atoms) and the symmetry of the atoms themselves.  

Thus, a **space group** is a set of points in the crystal structure that are identical to the origin due to the symmetry of the crystal.  

\boxed{\text{Space group = linear symmetry (translation and translation length) + translational symmetry (translation of the unit plane) + translational symmetry (translation of the atoms within the unit plane)}}",fluency,"# Task Description
