\]
where \( P_{\text{max}} \) is the maximum pressure and \( p_1 \) is the pressure at the beginning of compression.

Rearranging the equation:
\[
\frac{P_{\text{max}}}{p_1} = \frac{1}{1 - \epsilon} = \frac{1}{1 - 0.56} = \frac{1}{0.44} \approx 2.36 \).
\[
k = \frac{P_{\text{max}}}{p_1} = 2.36
\]

